  "findings": [
    "Cinemeta Jujutsu S2E1 and S3E1 thumbnail requests return HTTP 404; S1E1 thumbnail returns an image. The matching Nuvio Catalog S1E25/S1E48 images return HTTP 200.",
    "The primary API returns HTTP 404 for S2E1. Its S1E25 response contains two URLs at zebi.xalaflix.design, which are unreadable. The direct API supplies no replacement at the checked routes.",
    "The backup API uses a different layout: S2E1 has eight VF and eight VOSTFR candidates, whereas S1E25 is pending. The production S2E1 lookup returns two VOE VOSTFR choices, with one MP4 media sample passing and its HLS segment sample returning HTTP 403. The canonical-coordinate lookup returns zero.",
    "Globally rewriting the request from S2E1 to S1E25 would discard the currently available backup choices. No routing or source URLs were changed.",
    "The native plugin receives ID/type/season/episode, without the selected metadata provider or episode title/date. Overlapping coordinates cannot always reveal their originating catalogue.",
    "TMDB episode enrichment in the inspected Nuvio Mobile source matches the existing season/episode pair. It does not convert Cinemeta episode numbering. Sources FR and Anime-Sama stream plugins do not supply metadata page artwork.",
    "Do not treat the prior dedicated Anime-Sama missing-season fix as universal Sources FR or Cinemeta compatibility. Missing images, mismatched backend coordinates, expired/dead media and unsupported hosts need separate diagnoses."
  ],
